   "independent_transcript": "Yeah, so obviously at Red Belly, we've been always focused on how do we bring financial services on chain. And Liquidise has always been a great partner of Red Belly, and they've been focused specifically at the time on private equities. We saw the opportunity at Red Belly to broaden that and obviously focused on other alternate assets. But the key to everything is the registry. So who holds what? In a regulated environment, the bearer instrument is, other than cash, pretty much illegal now across every jurisdiction. So there is always regulatory required a registry. And so we've been working with Matt and saw the opportunity with some of other partners to greatly accelerate that adoption by helping them with already having a tokenized registry. So as Matt said, we've acquired Liquidize or the registry business and their customers. And we've now rebranded that into tokenizer, which is much more focused on a full cradle to grave, if you like, on asset origination, asset servicing and obviously registry. And then whatever wants to hear about, the secondary trading opportunities that will be unlocked. but we've got to start with us get the assets on.",
